    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2TjAz7AF8uUQoE1r8NCDGbJ)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Independent; builds on #533 and #536 (merged).\n\n## What changed\n\n- New option `sp-split-notes` for `sp-split-leave-parents` (in `sp-refile`), default `move`:\n  - the footnotes, see-also notes (`see-N`) and endnotes (`end-N`) that the split heading cites are written in the `Notes / Appendix` section of the new note, renumbered in its order (end notes, see-also notes, then footnotes)\n  - `move`: the source also loses the definitions that nothing left there cites any more, and is renumbered; the copy in the new note keeps the context\n  - `copy`: the source keeps everything\n  - `nil`: the older behaviour, a copy under each citing heading\n- A note that the remaining part of the source still cites stays in the source.\n- A note cited but defined nowhere is reported as before and left alone.\n- `sp-note--ordered` now keeps plain footnotes after the end/see notes.\n- Default changed for plain footnotes too: with `sp-split-notes` non-nil they go to the notes section instead of under each citing heading.\n\n## What was run\n\n- Emacs 29.3 batch: 3 new tests for the helpers (new note body, a body with its own definitions, taking notes out of a source after a cut) pass; `sp-note-kinds` tests pass.\n- `sp-refile-test` has one failing test (`sp-split-file-by-tags-moves-note-into-tag-folder`) that also fails on main.\n- Not run: a real split with vulpea (not installed in the container), so the wiring through `vulpea-split--write-file` and the cut is untested; the source buffer is changed and not saved.\n\n## Open questions\n\n- `move` is the default because you said to take the notes from one file to another; set `copy` if you would rather keep the source untouched.\n- A cited note with a missing definition is renumbered like the others (e.g. `see-9` becomes `see-2`).\n\n## Manual test checklist\n\n- [ ] Split a heading that cites a `see-` note, an `end-` note and a numbered footnote: the new note has `* Notes / Appendix` with end, see, then the footnote, renumbered from 1\n- [ ] The source no longer has the definitions that only that heading cited, and its remaining notes are renumbered (buffer unsaved)\n- [ ] A note also cited from the part that stays is still in the source\n- [ ] With `sp-split-notes` set to `copy`, the source keeps all definitions\n- [ ] With `sp-split-notes` set to nil, plain footnotes behave as before\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAHsMuLG5iLMWeAjmt)_",
